p=A.mr(j,h,g,f,e.dG(-54e9),!1,"demo_image_calm_sky","https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?w=1400&q=80",j,p.a,"Visual reflection \u2014 Alamiyah demo",B.cc,B.ahh,"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?w=800&q=80","Look up \u2014 a visual pause before dhikr","Before you scroll further, stay with this sky for twenty seconds. Soften the jaw. Unclench the hands. Then choose one short dhikr \u2014 Subhanallah, Alhamdulillah, or Allahu Akbar \u2014 and say it thirty-three times while the image is still in mind.\n\nVisual quiet is not empty. It is a doorway. Many of us arrive to remembrance already noisy. An image like this slows the entrance so the words have somewhere to land.\n\nIf tears come, let them. If nothing comes, that is also fine. The point is arriving, not performing feeling. When you are ready, open a text dua and continue. Carry a piece of this calm into the next screen.",j,B.hw)
o=A.iM(f).e[2]
o=A.mr("\u0648\u064e\u0627\u0635\u0652\u0628\u0650\u0631\u0652 \u0648\u064e\u0645\u064e\u0627 \u0635\u064e\u0628\u0652\u0631\u064f\u0643\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0628\u0650\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650",h,g,f,e.dG(-648e8),!1,"demo_image_masjid_light","https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564760055775-d63b17a55c44?w=1400&q=80",j,o.a,"Qur'an 16:127 \u2014 visual pairing",B.cc,B.ahi,"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564760055775-d63b17a55c44?w=800&q=80","Light on stone \u2014 patience in still frames","And be patient, and your patience is not but through Allah. (16:127)\n\nArchitecture teaches what hurry forgets: beauty is built slowly. Look at the lines of light. Imagine the hands that carved and cleaned and called to prayer here across years you will never meet.\n\nPatience is not passive waiting. It is active trust with a quiet face. Pair this image with the ayah above. Read it once for meaning, once for sound, once for the place in your life that needs sabr most.\n\nThen leave the phone for two minutes. Return only when the breath has lengthened. That small gap is the real content of this card.","Wasbir wa ma sabruka illa billah",B.hw)
n=A.iM(f).e[1]
n=A.mr(j,h,g,f,e.dG(-792e8),!1,"demo_image_ramadan_table","https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1578662996442-48f60103fc96?w=1400&q=80",j,n.a,j,B.cc,B.ajB,"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1578662996442-48f60103fc96?w=800&q=80","Dates and dusk \u2014 a Ramadan mood board for the heart","Ramadan is not only hunger and schedule. It is the soft hour when a table becomes a place of thanks. Stay with this image and name who you would invite if distance were nothing \u2014 living or passed \u2014 and make dua for them by name.\n\nGratitude deepens when it is specific. Not \u201calhamdulillah for everything,\u201d but alhamdulillah for this bread, this water, this chance to break a fast again.\n\nIf it is not Ramadan where you are, borrow the mood anyway. Fasting of the tongue and the eyes can begin on any calendar. Let the picture remind you that worship also looks like shared warmth.",j,B.hw)
m=A.iM("poems").e[0]
m=A.mr(j,h,g,"poems",e.dG(-936e8),!1,"demo_video_bee","https://flutter.github.io/assets-for-api-docs/assets/videos/bee.mp4",j,m.a,"Flutter sample asset (demo)",B.cc,B.akk,"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507003211169-0a1dd7228f2d?w=1200&q=80","A tiny reminder \u2014 watch, then breathe","This is a very small sample clip so you can test in-app playback. Watch once without multitasking. When it ends, close your eyes for three breaths and say: Subhanallahi wa bihamdihi.\n\nShort video can still be deep if you treat it as a ritual rather than a feed. After playback, return to a long text dua and stay there longer than the clip lasted. Let the moving image be a doorway, not the destination.\n\nIf the video fails to load, check your connection and open again. The point of this card is presence practice paired with motion \u2014 a contrast to static reading.",j,B.dV)
